    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but the design isn't just \"mathematical,\" it's hyper-specific. like, if you look at the wings of the airplane shape, the proportions aren't just for aesthetics; they mirror the geometry of phased array antennas. and the way the monuments are spaced... it's too calculated. why would they need such extreme, rigid symmetry if it was just for \"function\"? it feels like they're hiding the purpose in plain sight. if we ignore the \"official\" architectural brief and just treat the layout as a physical resonator, can we at least run some rough numbers on the resonant frequency based on the length of the main axis? just to see if it aligns with anything in the deep space spectrum?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
